## 🔄 1.1 Capture Page State (MANDATORY - NEW COMPONENTS ONLY)

### **Requirements**
- **(MANDATORY)** **SKIP this step for reusable components** identified in **[Phase 0](mdc:Phase0_ReusabilityAnalysis.mdc)**
- **(MANDATORY)** Use Playwright snapshot to research actual page structure for NEW components only
- **(MANDATORY)** Take snapshots of target pages before generating any locators for NEW components
- **(MANDATORY)** NEVER generate blind locators - all locators MUST be derived from real page snapshots

### **Actions**
- Navigate to target pages
- Use Playwright snapshot tool to capture page state
- Document page structure and layout
- Identify interactive elements

---

## 📋 1.2 Element HTML Collection (MANDATORY - NEW COMPONENTS ONLY)

### **Requirements**
- **(MANDATORY)** **SKIP this step for reusable components** identified in **[Phase 0](mdc:Phase0_ReusabilityAnalysis.mdc)**
- **(MANDATORY)** BEFORE any interaction with web page elements (buttons, links, inputs, etc.), use `browser_evaluate` to get the element's HTML code
- **(MANDATORY)** **Prefer VISIBLE controls** - prioritize collecting and using elements that are currently visible and interactable on screen
- **(MANDATORY)** **Verify control alignment with test description** - ensure controls used match the text/name mentioned in test description
- **(MANDATORY)** **Consider actual control types** - controls may have different HTML types than expected:
  - Buttons may be `<a href role="button">` instead of `<button>` type
  - Links may use different elements than standard `<a href ...>`
  - Always inspect actual HTML structure, not assumptions

### **Storage Requirements**
- **(MANDATORY)** Save ALL collected element HTML to `tests/Raw/Debug/ElementsCollected.ts` file
- **(MANDATORY)** Use the structure: `{ description, action, html, locatorSuggestion }`
- **(MANDATORY)** This file MUST be used as the source for creating `tests/Utils/locator_cache.json`
- **(MANDATORY)** Never interact with an element before collecting its HTML code
- **(MANDATORY)** Collect HTML for ALL interactive elements: buttons, links, inputs, selects, checkboxes, radio buttons, textareas, etc.
- **(MANDATORY)** **Store page investigation sequence** - document all steps, findings, and decisions during page research in `tests/Raw/Debug/` folder

### **Table View Context**
- **(MANDATORY)** When working with table views, ensure collected controls belong to the correct table (important when multiple tables exist on same page)

