## 🎯 1.3 Locator Generation from Real Data (MANDATORY - NEW COMPONENTS ONLY)

### **Requirements**
- **(MANDATORY)** **SKIP this step for reusable components** identified in **[Phase 0](mdc:Phase0_ReusabilityAnalysis.mdc)** - use existing locators from cache
- **(MANDATORY)** DO NOT generate locators not based on actual page state for NEW components
- **(MANDATORY)** All NEW locators must be derived from real page snapshots and collected element HTML
- **(MANDATORY)** The `locatorSuggestion` field from `ElementsCollected.ts` MUST be used directly as the `locator` value in `locator_cache.json`
- **(MANDATORY)** Verify locator accuracy against captured page state
- **(MANDATORY)** No guessing - always collect actual HTML first for NEW components

### **Locator Generation Rules (for locatorSuggestion field)**
Reference: [Playwright Locator Best Practices](https://playwright.dev/docs/locators)

**Priority Order**:

**1. Text-based selectors (HIGHEST PRIORITY)**:
   - `button:has-text("Sign In")` - for buttons with text
   - `a:has-text("Company Info")` - for links with text
   - `:has-text("exact text")` - for elements with specific text

**2. Form field selectors by placeholder**:
   - `input[placeholder="Email *"]` - for inputs with placeholder
   - `input[placeholder="First Name *"]` - clear and stable

**3. Attribute-based selectors**:
   - `input[name="username"]` - for form inputs with name
   - `input[type="submit"][name="login"]` - combine type and name
   - `a[href="/e-care/company-info"]` - for links by href

**4. Role-based selectors**:
   - `[role="tab"]:has-text("Users")` - for tabs with text
   - `[role="button"]:has-text("Create")` - for role buttons

**5. ID selectors (use cautiously)**:
   - `#username` - only if ID is stable and meaningful
   - Avoid auto-generated IDs like `#rc-tabs-0-tab-users`

**6. Class selectors (LOWEST PRIORITY)**: 
   - `button[class*="ant-btn-icon-only"]` - only when no better option
   - Use `*=` for partial class match to handle dynamic classes

**AVOID**:
- ❌ Long complex selectors with multiple classes
- ❌ Overly specific paths: `div.container > div.row > button.primary`
- ❌ Dynamic classes that change on each run
- ❌ Index-based selectors unless absolutely necessary

**EXAMPLES OF GOOD LOCATORS**:
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Simple, readable, stable
locatorSuggestion: 'button:has-text("Log In")'
locatorSuggestion: 'input[name="username"]'
locatorSuggestion: 'input[placeholder="Email *"]'
locatorSuggestion: 'a[href="/e-care/company-info"]'
locatorSuggestion: '[role="tab"]:has-text("Users")'

// ❌ BAD - Too complex, unstable
locatorSuggestion: 'button.ant-btn.css-t2kvhy.ant-btn-default.ant-btn-color-default.ant-btn-variant-outlined.KJuB2.taButton.RMLC5.GK8tV'
locatorSuggestion: 'div[role="tab"][id="rc-tabs-0-tab-users"] div.taTab:has-text("Users")'
```

---

## 🎨 Dynamic Elements - Use `{param}` Placeholder

For elements identified by **runtime data** (user names, item names, dynamic text):

**locatorSuggestion with `{param}`**:
```typescript
// Row by data: 'tr:has(strong:has-text("{param}")) a.btn-outline-info i.fa-eye'
// Button by text: 'button:has-text("{param}")'
// In container: 'div:has(h3:has-text("{param}")) button.action'
```

**Use `{param}` when**: Element ID depends on test data (names, IDs from scenario)  
**Don't use when**: Element has unique static locator (name, ID, class)

